  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj` is regenerated with the documented command `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test first_4axis_part`.\n- The diff has 6 lines: the file `version` (62 to 63) and the `stamp` of each of the five operations.\n- The cached moves do not change.\n- `examples/first-4axis-part.nc` does not change. The posted G-code is byte-identical.\n- No code changes.\n\n## Cause\n\n- PR #2155 (#2152) changed the stamp salt to `camcraft-op-stamp-v3`. The intent: an old cache reads stale one time, and the post refuses it until a regenerate.\n- PR #2135 saved the example on a branch without PR #2155, thus with v2 stamps.\n- After the two merges, the machine check refused the example: `Flat A-90: inputs moved since generation - regenerate before posting`.\n- The refusal is the correct output. The example file was stale. The bisect and the readings are on the issue.\n- `main` is red from `4b7a6b1e8` (run 43870387249), not only from `e3ca44fa7` (run 43899170442).\n\n## Tests\n\n- `first_4axis_part` (all 4 tests), debug, on this head: pass.\n  - `the_committed_project_posts_the_committed_program`: the pinning test. It fails on `origin/main` and passes here.\n  - `the_first_4axis_part_posts_its_indexed_program`: the program is equal to the committed `.nc`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `site/tests/test_first_4axis_part.py`: pytest is not installed on this machine. The `.nc` that the page quotes does not change.\n- The full batch tier. The post-merge gate runs it after the merge.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2198\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
